\f0\b \cf0 House analogy used in class:
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
LangGraph = the blueprint and load-bearing structure. You build from scratch.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
LangChain = a house where the base exists and you decide the rooms.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Deep Agents = move-in ready. Planning, virtual file system, sub-agents, and context compression come pre-wired. Built on top of LangChain agents.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Kitchen analogy for why the course starts with LangChain, not Deep Agents:
\f1\b0  starting at Deep Agents is like taking a chef's job when all you can do is order from Swiggy. You get food, but you control nothing. LangChain is the kitchen. LangGraph is buying the vegetables too.\

\f0\b LangFuse is not part of LangChain.
\f1\b0  It is an independent open-source AI engineering platform that happens to have "lang" in the name.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 LangSmith\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Reading agent code does not tell you what the agent did at runtime. You need the 
\f0\b trace
\f1\b0 : when the model was called, which tool fired, what happened in middleware, tokens consumed, time taken, and where it failed. LangSmith is the flight's black box. Compare it to logging for ordinary code.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Agent = Model + Harness\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The central formula of the class.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\f0\b model
\f1\b0  (LLM) is the engine or brain. Powerful, but useless alone: stateless, no memory of you, cannot send an email, has no idea what tools exist.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The 
\f0\b harness
\f1\b0  is everything you wrap around it: system prompt, tools, middleware, guardrails, checkpoints, memory, sub-agents, context.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Harness engineering
\f1\b0  is the current term for doing this well.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Claude Code and ChatGPT are agent applications: a strong model at the center, plus connectors, skills, memory, and web search harnessing it.\
Corollary raised in class: don't run the cheapest model and expect the smartest agent. Capability of the agent depends on the brain, then on how well you harness it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

