\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Sanity check\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 from langchain.agents import create_agent\
\
def get_weather(city: str) -> str:\
    """Get weather for a given city."""\
    return f"It's always sunny in \{city\}!"\
\
agent = create_agent(\
    model="openai:gpt-5.5",\
    tools=[get_weather],\
    system_prompt="You are a helpful assistant",\
)\
agent.invoke(\{"messages": [\{"role": "user", "content": "What is the weather in SF?"\}]\})\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Important behaviour:
\f1\b0  LangChain reads the provider's conventional environment variable automatically. Set 
\f2\fs26 OPENAI_API_KEY
\f1\fs24  and the OpenAI model just works. Switch the model to Anthropic without setting 
\f2\fs26 ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
\f1\fs24  and you get an authentication error ("could not resolve authentication method"). Rename the variable to something like 
\f2\fs26 OPENAI_2
\f1\fs24  and it breaks.\
