\cf0 Swapping providers means rewriting the call, the message format, and the response parsing. LangChain standardizes all of it, so changing models is a one-line edit. That matters when a new model appears (Kimi, MiniMax, whatever launches next) and you want to test it without rewriting the app.\
Official philosophy page, condensed: LLMs are powerful; they get better when combined with external data and tools; they change what applications look like.\
The same pattern repeats in every framework. CrewAI has its own 
\f2\fs26 LLM
\f1\fs24  class doing exactly this job. Learning LangChain deeply makes CrewAI, ADK, Strands, and Agent SDK quick to pick up (Hindi-then-English grammar analogy).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \
